It can be worked around, but it is not trivial and prone to error. Currently, we must write custom validation logic for every single exported field, often involving reflection or parsing SceneState.
```c#
private PackedScene _scene;
[Export]
public PackedScene MyScene
{
    get => _scene;
    set
    {
        if (value != null) {
            var state = value.GetState();
            // Complex logic to parse state.GetNodePropertyValue(0, "script") ...
            if (!IsTypeMatch(state, typeof(MyType))) {
                GD.PrintErr("Invalid type");
                _scene = null;
                return;
            }
        }
        _scene = value;
    }
}
```
This is too much friction for a feature (Type Safety).
